# GitHub workflow — PR Lens

Before opening or updating a pull request, follow `.agents/skills/pr-lens/SKILL.md`
(Claude Code follows the identical copy at `.claude/skills/pr-lens/SKILL.md`):

- Diff against the merge base, not the tip of `main`.
- Write `.pr-lens/graph.json`, then run
  `npx @coldtea/pr-lens-cli@latest validate .pr-lens/graph.json`, then
  `npx @coldtea/pr-lens-cli@latest render .pr-lens/graph.json --theme light`.
- Show the rendered diagrams and say in a few lines what they show before
  opening or updating the pull request — wait for confirmation first.
- Pull request body: one sentence on why, then the architecture diagram.
  Add a data-flow diagram only when there is a sequence worth walking
  through. Attach with `gh pr create` or `gh pr edit --attach`.
- Do not commit `.pr-lens/` — the CLI already adds it to `.gitignore`.
  Corrections to a diagram go in `.github/pr-lens.yml`, never in the
  generated SVGs.

Claude Code follows the same rule via `CLAUDE.md`. If you edit the skill
itself, keep `.claude/skills/pr-lens` and `.agents/skills/pr-lens`
identical — they're separate copies, one per agent, not linked.
